{=============================================================================
  Reciprocating compressor from catalogue data (R717)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0157 - native file (BLOCKED)
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Isentropic and volumetric effectiveness of an R717 reciprocating compressor
  computed directly from manufacturer (catalogue) data: the catalogue rows
  (condensing/evaporating temperature, capacity, electrical power, mass flow)
  are read from a lookup table and turned into epsilon_s and epsilon_v versus
  pressure ratio, plus a power-law extrapolation of epsilon_s to 1000/750 rpm.
  STATUS: blocked - CS-BUG-DUPLICATE-VAR-BOUND (DUPLICATE i=1,n dropped),
  CS-GAP-LOOKUP-NONAME (nameless lookup(i,col) rejected). Run the verified
  variant reciprocating_catalogue_r717_coolsolve.eescode (README.md).
  Inputs : lookup table (17 rows), fluid$, V_s_cp, rpm_cp, rpm2, rpm3,
           DELTAT_oh, m; Outputs: epsilon_s_cp_mes[i], epsilon_v_cp_mes[i],
           R_p_cp[i], epsilon_s_1000_rpm[i], epsilon_s_750_rpm[i]
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : Laborelec compressor toolkit 2002, F. Trebilcock (ULiège) - README.md
=============================================================================}

"!MODEL"
"The model obtains the curves of the isentropic and volumetric effectiveness
 directly from the manufacturer information. The catalogue data (compressor
 selection software) go into the lookup table of the model; given the swept
 volume of the compressor, its rotational speed and the superheating at which
 the data were taken, the effectiveness can be plotted versus the pressure
 ratio (plots 1 and 2 of the original file). As in the original."

n = 17                          "number of rows in the lookup table [-]"
DUPLICATE i = 1, n

"Measured effectiveness"
w_mes[i] = W_dot_cp_mes[i]/M_dot_cp_mes[i]               "measured specific work [J/kg]"
epsilon_s_cp_mes[i] = w_s[i]/w_mes[i]                    "global isentropic effectiveness [-]"
V_dot_su_cp_mes[i] = M_dot_cp_mes[i]*v_su_cp[i]          "suction volume flow rate [m^3/s]"
epsilon_v_cp_mes[i] = V_dot_su_cp_mes[i]/V_dot_sw_cp[i]  "global volumetric effectiveness [-]"

w_s[i] = h_exs_cp[i] - h_su_cp[i]                        "isentropic specific work [J/kg]"
V_dot_sw_cp[i] = V_s_cp*N_cp[i]                          "displaced volume flow rate [m^3/s]"
N_cp[i] = rpm_cp/60                                      "rotational speed [1/s]"

R_p_cp[i] = p_ex_cp[i]/p_su_cp[i]                        "pressure ratio [-]"

"Fluid definition"
h_exs_cp[i] = enthalpy(fluid$, p=p_ex_cp[i], s=s_su_cp[i])  "isentropic exhaust enthalpy [J/kg]"
h_su_cp[i] = enthalpy(fluid$, t=t_su_cp[i], p=p_su_cp[i])   "supply enthalpy [J/kg]"
s_su_cp[i] = entropy(fluid$, t=t_su_cp[i], p=p_su_cp[i])    "supply entropy [J/kg-K]"
v_su_cp[i] = volume(fluid$, t=t_su_cp[i], p=p_su_cp[i])     "supply specific volume [m^3/kg]"

"Measured outputs (manufacturer data)"
W_dot_cp_mes[i] = lookup(i, 4)                           "electrical power [W]"
M_dot_cp_mes[i] = lookup(i, 5)                           "mass flow rate [kg/s]"

"Saturation pressures and supply state"
P_cd[i] = PRESSURE(fluid$, T=T_cd[i], X=1)               "condensation pressure [Pa]"
P_ev[i] = PRESSURE(fluid$, T=T_ev[i], X=1)               "evaporation pressure [Pa]"
t_su_cp[i] = T_ev[i] + DELTAT_oh                         "supply temperature [°C]"
p_su_cp[i] = P_ev[i]
p_ex_cp[i] = P_cd[i]

"Catalogue inputs (one row per operating point)"
T_cd[i] = lookup(i, 1)                                   "condensing temperature [°C]"
T_ev[i] = lookup(i, 2)                                   "evaporating temperature [°C]"

"Effectiveness extrapolated to other speeds (as in the original)"
epsilon_s_1000_rpm[i] = epsilon_s_cp_mes[i]*(rpm_cp/rpm2)^m
epsilon_s_750_rpm[i] = epsilon_s_cp_mes[i]*(rpm_cp/rpm3)^m
END

"Constant inputs"
fluid$ = 'R717'                 "refrigerant"
V_s_cp = 0.0009712              "swept volume [m^3] (recommended: use the manufacturer swept volume)"
rpm_cp = 1450                   "rotational speed of the catalogue data [rpm]"
rpm2 = 1000                     "speed of the 1000 rpm curve [rpm]"
rpm3 = 750                      "speed of the 750 rpm curve [rpm]"
DELTAT_oh = 5.001               "superheating at which the data were taken [K]"
m = 0.18                        "exponent of the speed correction [-]"

"Inactive in the active model (nested-brace comment of the original): an
 alternative evaporator balance computing Q_dot_ev[i] from the cycle
 (condenser outlet subcooled by DELTAT_sc, then Q_dot_ev = M_dot*(h_su_cp -
 h_ex_cd)) instead of reading it from the catalogue; it also contains the
 commented input DELTAT_sc = 0.001 [K]. Curve-fitting expression noted in the
 original: epsilon_s_cp_mes[i] = a0 + a1*(R_p_cp[i]-7)^2 + a2/(R_p_cp[i]-a3)
 (coefficients a0..a3 are not defined in this file)."
